<body>
<div class="poster">

  <!-- HEADER -->
  <div class="header">
    <div class="header-tag">World Bank &nbsp;|&nbsp; Global Economic Prospects</div>
    <div class="header-badge">
      <div class="hb-num">6</div>
      <div class="hb-label">Decades</div>
      <div class="hb-label" style="font-size:11px;margin-top:3px;color:#fde68a;">Strongest Recovery</div>
    </div>
    <h1>Resilience<br><em>Amid Uncertainty</em></h1>
    <p class="header-sub">The global economy staged its strongest post-recession recovery in six decades — yet this resilience is uneven. Vulnerable emerging markets lag behind as escalating trade tensions and policy uncertainty threaten the outlook.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- BODY -->
  <div class="body">

    <!-- SECTION 1: RECOVERY -->
    <div class="section">
      <div class="section-tag" style="background:#dbeafe;color:#1d4ed8;">01 &nbsp; Recovery</div>
      <h2>A Historic — But <span class="accent">Uneven</span> — Recovery</h2>

      <div class="recovery-highlight">
        <div class="rh-stat">
          <div class="big">6</div>
          <div class="unit">Decades</div>
        </div>
        <div class="rh-text">
          Last year's faster-than-expected growth capped a recovery from the 2020 recession <strong>unmatched in six decades</strong>. However, current-year growth is projected to edge downward as firms draw down front-loaded inventories and tariff effects intensify.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="divergence-row">
        <div class="div-card advanced">
          <div class="dc-label">Advanced Economies</div>
          <div class="dc-body">Robust momentum continues, supported by resilient labor markets and consumption. Policy space largely intact.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="div-card vulnerable">
          <div class="dc-label">Vulnerable EMDEs</div>
          <div class="dc-body">Persistently lagging behind. Tight financing conditions, commodity exposure, and structural bottlenecks deepen the divergence.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- SECTION 2: RISKS -->
    <div class="section">
      <div class="section-tag" style="background:#fee2e2;color:#dc2626;">02 &nbsp; Risks</div>
      <h2>Key <span class="accent">Risks</span> to the Outlook</h2>

      <div class="risk-grid">
        <div class="risk-item primary">
          <span class="ri-badge">Top Risk</span>
          <span class="ri-icon">⚠️</span>
          <div class="ri-title">Trade Tensions &amp; Tariffs</div>
          <div class="ri-body">Escalating tariffs and retaliatory measures disrupt supply chains and dampen business investment — the most policy-relevant risk for this cycle.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="risk-item primary">
          <span class="ri-badge">High Impact</span>
          <span class="ri-icon">📉</span>
          <div class="ri-title">Financial Market Volatility</div>
          <div class="ri-body">Deteriorating sentiment could sharply tighten financing conditions, disproportionately hitting vulnerable EMDEs with limited fiscal buffers.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="risk-item secondary">
          <span class="ri-icon">📦</span>
          <div class="ri-title">Inventory Correction</div>
          <div class="ri-body">Firms that front-loaded purchases are now drawing down stocks, reducing near-term demand and contributing to a growth slowdown.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="risk-item secondary">
          <span class="ri-icon">🌡️</span>
          <div class="ri-title">Climate Shocks</div>
          <div class="ri-body">Extreme weather events threaten agricultural output and infrastructure, amplifying economic volatility in the most exposed regions.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- SECTION 3: POLICY -->
    <div class="section full-width">
      <div class="section-tag" style="background:#dcfce7;color:#16a34a;">03 &nbsp; Policy Actions</div>
      <h2>Policy Actions for <span class="accent">Sustained Growth</span></h2>
      <table class="policy-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Reform Area</th>
            <th>Global Action</th>
            <th>Domestic Action</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><span class="area-badge">Trade</span></td>
            <td>Improve the multilateral trade environment; reduce fragmentation</td>
            <td>Diversify trade partners and products to reduce concentration risk</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><span class="area-badge">Finance</span></td>
            <td>Ease external financing constraints for EMDEs; expand multilateral lending</td>
            <td>Strengthen macroeconomic policy frameworks and fiscal credibility</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><span class="area-badge">Climate</span></td>
            <td>Scale up climate risk mitigation and adaptation finance</td>
            <td>Invest in resilient infrastructure and climate-smart agriculture</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><span class="area-badge">Investment</span></td>
            <td>Catalyze private capital flows into developing economies</td>
            <td>Remove structural bottlenecks to business entry and productivity</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><span class="area-badge">Jobs</span></td>
            <td>Support cross-border labor mobility to match skills with demand</td>
            <td>Enhance skills development and labor market flexibility for youth</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <!-- SECTION 4: 2030 TARGETS -->
    <div class="section full-width">
      <div class="section-tag" style="background:#fef3c7;color:#b45309;">04 &nbsp; Strategic Priorities</div>
      <h2>World Bank <span class="accent">2030</span> Strategic Priorities</h2>

      <div class="targets-intro">
        <div class="ti-stat">
          <div class="big">1.2B</div>
          <div class="unit">Youth</div>
        </div>
        <div class="ti-text">
          <strong>1.2 billion young people</strong> will reach working age in the next decade, placing job creation and inclusive growth at the center of the World Bank Group's mission and 2030 flagship targets.
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="targets-grid">
        <div class="target-card">
          <span class="tc-icon">🏥</span>
          <div class="tc-value">1.5B</div>
          <div class="tc-initiative">Health Services</div>
          <div class="tc-desc">Quality, affordable health services delivered to 1.5 billion people</div>
        </div>
        <div class="target-card">
          <span class="tc-icon">⚡</span>
          <div class="tc-value">300M</div>
          <div class="tc-initiative">Mission 300 — Electricity</div>
          <div class="tc-desc">Electricity access for 300 million people in Sub-Saharan Africa</div>
        </div>
        <div class="target-card">
          <span class="tc-icon">🌾</span>
          <div class="tc-value">300M</div>
          <div class="tc-initiative">AgriConnect</div>
          <div class="tc-desc">300 million farmers helped up the agricultural value chain</div>
        </div>
        <div class="target-card">
          <span class="tc-icon">💼</span>
          <div class="tc-value">80M</div>
          <div class="tc-initiative">Women's Capital</div>
          <div class="tc-desc">80 million women &amp; women-led businesses with capital access</div>
        </div>
        <div class="target-card">
          <span class="tc-icon">💧</span>
          <div class="tc-value">1B+</div>
          <div class="tc-initiative">Water Forward</div>
          <div class="tc-desc">Water security for 1B+ people; 400M World Bank Group commitment</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- SECTION 5: RESEARCH THEMES -->
    <div class="section full-width">
      <div class="section-tag" style="background:#ede9fe;color:#7c3aed;">05 &nbsp; Research Themes</div>
      <h2>Key Research Themes in <span class="accent">Recent Issues</span></h2>
      <div class="themes-grid">
        <div class="theme-card">
          <span class="th-icon">📊</span>
          <div class="th-title">Fiscal Policy</div>
          <div class="th-topics">Rebuilding fiscal space through fiscal rules (Jan 2026); fiscal challenges in small states (Jun 2024)</div>
        </div>
        <div class="theme-card">
          <span class="th-icon">🚢</span>
          <div class="th-title">Trade &amp; Supply Chains</div>
          <div class="th-topics">High trade costs — causes and remedies (Jun 2021); COVID-19 impact on global value chains (Jun 2020)</div>
        </div>
        <div class="theme-card">
          <span class="th-icon">🛢️</span>
          <div class="th-title">Commodity Markets</div>
          <div class="th-topics">Commodity price cycles — drivers and policies (Jan 2022); Russia-Ukraine energy implications (Jun 2022)</div>
        </div>
        <div class="theme-card">
          <span class="th-icon">🏦</span>
          <div class="th-title">Financial Spillovers</div>
          <div class="th-topics">Rising U.S. interest rates (Jun 2023); fourth wave of rapid debt buildup (Jan 2020)</div>
        </div>
        <div class="theme-card">
          <span class="th-icon">🦠</span>
          <div class="th-title">Pandemic Economics</div>
          <div class="th-topics">COVID-19 impact on global income inequality (Jan 2022); regional macroeconomic implications (Jun 2020)</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div><!-- /body -->

  <!-- FOOTER -->
  <div class="footer">
    <div class="footer-left">
      <strong>World Bank Group — Global Economic Prospects</strong>
      Data and analysis drawn from the Global Economic Prospects report series &nbsp;·&nbsp; worldbank.org/gep
    </div>
    <div class="footer-right">
      <div class="footer-tag">2025 Edition</div>
      <div>Policy Intelligence &nbsp;|&nbsp; Emerging Markets &nbsp;|&nbsp; Development Finance</div>
    </div>
  </div>

</div><!-- /poster -->
</body>
</html>
